module gunbc.plans.names_without_imports

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol, quote }

fn names_without_imports_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    h2(text: "Resolved-declaration evaluation prerequisite, authorized 2026-11-20"),
    p(text: "What: the seed evaluates a bound callable by that declaration, including when it is passed as a value. An explicit declaration binding precedes ambient spelling dispatch; an unrelated declaration merely present in the closure supplies no binding. The existing std.primitive_projection::ProjectionFidelity and v1.std.core::CallTargetIdentity carry the decision: HostRealizedSeam requires its host realization, ModeledProjection may evaluate its declared body when the realization is absent, and DivergentProjection or an unprojected declaration evaluates its own body. The interpreter consumes the same resolved_declaration_call_target as Rust emission instead of creating another projection roster. Existing reflection bridges likewise require the selected declaration's owner, never the closure-wide bare-name registry."),
    p(text: "Why: the whole-list std.host_text::text_of_chars admission cannot remove its native chars_to_string dependency while its seed realization is selected by spelling. A local bridge can hijack an unrelated same-named function; retaining the old body avoids that defect but does not complete the native fix. Operator decision msg_6013f1ed-c034-4f29-8a8d-381a1bdceef4 authorizes this prerequisite. It serves the namespace intention and v2 self-hosting, not an expansion of seed language semantics."),
    p(text: "Done when: executed controls distinguish the host declaration from a same-named source declaration, an unrelated host module in the closure, a qualified call and a callable local binding; a required realization cannot silently execute its self-call body. The existing char_at absence probes are reconciled with the corrected declared contract. The whole-list crossing retains empty and Unicode round trips and refuses malformed scalar representations. Bootstrap regeneration converges before the admitted body becomes a self-call, and the native prepare probe demonstrates removal of the chars_to_string stop. A model-only or Rust-runtime-only admission does not satisfy this intention."),
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`). The work items live under the `namespace-unique-on-chain` project in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority` and name this intention; this plan does not list them."),
      p(text: "**Grounding:** `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority` (one name, one way to decide it; the name-to-path mapping runs one way), `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration` (the old authority ends in one motion at its root), `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization`, `gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate`, `gunbc.design_argument::epistemic_humility`."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** every reference to a declaration is spelled by its fully qualified path, all the time (`gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified`, 2026-11-17); a bare name is a lexical binder and nothing else; and the import concept is gone from the language: no import grammar, no import list, no import closure deciding the compiled population, no import retry, no bare-name pool, no ambient table, no candidate search, and no second deciding mechanism in the seed. Source enters as a bundle at one ingest step that parses it into a universe of declarations and discards the files (`gunbc.design_ruling::source_is_ingested_into_one_universe_and_files_are_discarded`): there is no module or namespace header, each declaration spells its own full path, and a file is a bag of declarations with no meaning. The closure of a compilation subject is the declaration-demand fixed point: authored qualified references seed it, compiler-generated demands (conversion routes, list and map heads, template heads, canonical operations, target support; `std.generated_provider`) extend it, and reading a file is the ingest step's realization of those demands, never a semantic fact. Authored name search is gone; what remains typed is exact-identity admission: no declaration at a path, two providers for one path, an unreadable artifact, a refused declaration, a path that is both a prefix and a declaration. Sugar for human authors, if any, is a later addition on top of this rule."),
    p(text: "**Why (operator, 2026-11-16):** imports cause a lot of problems, and by the time v2 is accepted they must be gone for good. The problems are on record: a file that declares any import silently gets no bare edges, so the compiled population is decided by accident (`namespace-v2-import-completion`); the symbol index is built from a tree-wide census while the compiled population is the import closure, two answers to what a name sees; and a name answered two ways by two code paths is this project's own red control. The operator also recorded that the project has been consistently mishandled, mostly by the operator: it has been re-scoped at least four times (the staged XL migration program withdrawn 2026-11-10, import-grammar deletion withdrawn 2026-11-08, re-admitted 2026-11-16), so this plan fixes the intention first and lets the realization be redrawn under it."),
    p(text: "**Three mechanisms answer a name today, and this intention leaves one.** (a) A declaration reached by lexical scope, an explicit import or a qualified path, the 2026-11-08 binding rule. (b) The resolver's four stopgap tables (`v2.compiler.resolve` `AmbientBindingTable`: the kernel type-spelling table, the kernel's canonical symbols, the std.primitives last tier, the collection roster), each recorded per occurrence as `BoundAmbient` and driven to deletion by the ambient-name census under the 2026-10-15 ruling that there are no built-ins and no prelude (`cross-module-declarations`'s boundary; the private ledger of gunb-ai/gunbc-private#289 counted 201 ambient-name rows on 2026-11-08). (c) The v1 seed's own built-ins, which answer the same sources a second way (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::an_unimported_bare_name_binds_differently_per_realization`). The ambient waves now landing (string_length, substring, char_at into `std.host_text`; fold, flat_map, first, last into `std.algebra`) are durable under this intention, because every name needs one declared home whatever reaches it; what is not durable is any investment in the reaching mechanism of (a), an import list that binds or an import retry, since the cut deletes it. The waves therefore continue, scoped to the native-seven closure first (161 of the compiler's 273 modules, by gunb-ai/gunbc-private#289's measurement), and the import-list machinery is frozen."),
    p(text: "**Done when** (each assessed against the tree unless marked as the operator's judgement):"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "The import production has been removed from both grammars. Both parsers reject a `.dag` file containing an import line with a located diagnostic naming the qualified-path spelling that replaces it."),
      li(text: "Every declaration reference in the corpus is fully qualified, and a bare head that no lexical binder answers refuses as unbound, located; the kernel (`namespace-binding-kernel`) admits exactly one provider for a path and refuses, typed, on none or on two (`namespace-ambiguity-discharge` closes: its remaining population is duplicate providers, which are malformed states, never a choice)."),
      li(text: "A subject's closure is the declaration-demand fixed point over authored and compiler-generated demands (`namespace-reference-derived-closure`, `std.generated_provider`), identical whichever unrelated declarations the universe holds; the ingest step realizes it by reading, and the seed loads by the same demands."),
      li(text: "No file-level semantic unit remains: no `module` header, no per-file policy row (each policy fact names the smallest subject it governs: the declaration, the namespace prefix, or the subject), and moving a declaration between files changes nothing."),
      li(text: "At production admission the qualified resolver alone decides declaration references. A production reference that only the bootstrap mirror could answer must refuse."),
      li(text: "`native-production-admission` consumes these receipts under `gunbc.design_ruling::v2_landing_waits_on_the_namespace_program` and `gunbc.design_ruling::imports_are_deleted_before_v2_is_accepted`. At interpreter retirement, `namespace-legacy-choice-retirement` verifies the physical removal of the unused seed mirror and the zero inventory of legacy mechanisms (`gunbc.design_ruling::production_namespace_admission_precedes_seed_mirror_removal`)."),
      li(text: "Operator's judgement: the corpus reads better without imports than with them; a migration that merely moved the import lists into longer spellings at every reference has not achieved this."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "2. The backward structure, read at e346a2c89daa"),
    p(text: "The project's eleven members declare no edges among themselves, so this is read from their texts. Each layer states what must already be true for the one above it."),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**The goal.** No import grammar, and the compiled population derived from references. This is the last cut, because deleting the grammar before every name binds without it would refuse the whole corpus at once."),
      li(text: "**Just before the grammar cut.** Every ordinary consumer uses the qualified resolver. The seed mirror’s later removal is verified with interpreter retirement."),
      li(text: "**Before that.** Every reference carries its declaration (`declaration-identity-switchover`), which needs the kernel (`namespace-binding-kernel`), exact occurrence identity (`namespace-occurrence-transport`), what a name can see from where it is written (`namespace-structural-observations`), dependencies derived from references (`namespace-reference-derived-closure`, with its producer bounded by `namespace-reference-derived-producer-bounded`), and the genuinely-many cases settled (`namespace-ambiguity-discharge`). `namespace-v2-import-completion`'s question (does an import list bind?) is answered by this intention: it does not; the import list is deleted, and in-scope is the switch-over's single definition."),
      li(text: "**Why name debt lands green today.** The required job has no native resolve step (gunb-ai/gunbc-private#289), so a landing that leaves a name ambient or unhomed passes CI and the next native-seven run finds it; site repairs were about twelve percent of migration commits and nothing held the line after a class-level fix. The operator ruled on 2026-11-16 that no ratchet is built for this (`gunbc.design_ruling::no_ratchets_names_bind_now_and_meaning_migrates_later`); what holds the line is a simple falsifiable reading used with judgment, section 7, until native resolve over the compiler closures refuses a bare or ambiguous name outright."),
      li(text: "**The scale, measured.** The 2026-11-16 parse sweep counts 10343 modules and about 292,000 import members. Every one of those lines is rewritten or made unnecessary by this program, so the realization is a generated rewrite through one generator over the whole corpus, never a hand migration, and it lands as one cut at the root with the generator as its offline differential oracle (`gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration`)."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Today's frontier**, read the same way: the kernel, occurrence transport and structural observations are the roots; the bounded producer is gated on gunb-ai/gunbc#11683 and gunb-ai/gunbc#11574 by its own text; `declaration-provider-outcomes` is also a parent of `native-seven` and is the member whose landing moves both intentions at once."),
    h2(text: "3. Layers of cleanup, prioritized against the goals (operator, 2026-11-17, re-cut the same day under the fully-qualified rule)"),
    p(text: "The operator's staging rule: cleanup is layered, and each layer is justified by the goal it unblocks, read backward from `gunbc.plans.v2_self_host`. Under `gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified` the layers simplify: there is no binding rule to design, no candidate population, no collision to discharge (two declarations with one spelling in two modules have two paths), and no temporary import to add and later delete. What remains per layer is one mechanical rewrite by the generator (every declaration reference to its resolved path, with the current import semantics as the oracle) plus the homes that names with no declaration still need. A compatible declaration needs only a resolved-path rewrite; a different label, carrier or contract needs its own compatibility evidence. The 2026-11-16 reading counts spellings and sites, not missing implementations: declarations under a different name and existing policy rows must be credited. Detailed realization and effort belong to gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_decomposition::roadmap_decompositions."),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Layer 0, the rule, the universe and the loader; serves every goal.** v2 resolves a declaration reference only through its qualified door, a bare head is a lexical binder or unbound, the four ambient tables are deleted, and the closure is the declaration-demand fixed point seeded by the authored references and extended by the compiler's generated demands. The ingest step parses the bundle into the universe and keeps only the text mapping. The seed loads by the same demands (its closure is import-derived today, `declared_import_closure`), which is the one seed change the program needs and the first thing to measure. Under `gunbc.design_ruling::operations_are_declarations_with_realizations` the collection roster, the kernel spelling tables, the primitive contracts and the CanonicalOperation enum converge here too: an operation is a declaration with a realization row, and an operator lowers to a reference to it."),
      li(text: "**Layer 1, native-seven passes (the operator's near-term milestone; gates `second-generation`).** every non-roster call bound to its declared contract in the native-seven closure (the historical reading counted 54 spellings across 161 modules, not 54 missing contracts; starts_with 28 sites, first 28, split 27, replace 18, to_string 13, code_point 10, then the tail), and the generator rewriting every declaration reference in the closure to its path, imports removed from those modules in the same landing. No import is added anywhere; the `contains` collision is no collision under the rule."),
      li(text: "**Layer 2, the compiler closures emit and build natively (`second-generation`, the emitter chain).** the compiler closures bind to declared contracts and are rewritten. The historical 80-name, 2,316-site reading is the larger closure population, not 80 additional homes: contracts covered in layer 1 and existing mappings such as sort_by are reused. Only the remaining contract differences are additional semantic work. The dual dag std declarations under src/v2/std (String, Int, UInt8, PositiveInt, FilePath, Unit, SourceSpan, TerminationProof) no longer gate anything here, since each has its own path; their merge stays owed to the 2026-10-18 kernel-type layer rule as its own work, accepted on its own evidence."),
      li(text: "**Layer 3, v2 is admitted as the production route (`native-production-admission`).** every remaining corpus call bound to its declared contract, with production, test and fixture modules rewritten. The historical 432-spelling, 46,923-site reading does not establish 432 new functions beyond the earlier layers; existing aliases and no-caller host exports are not missing implementations. The 5,910 production modules describe verification scope, not independent manual jobs. Then the import production leaves the grammar and the 75,782 import lines leave the tree in one landing, with the generator as the offline oracle (`gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration`). The 1,617 import members that would have been ambiguous are not a population under the rule; the reading retires that column."),
      li(text: "**Layer 3, also: the per-file policy rows.** The 2,374 `live_tree_disposition`, 1,165 `extdeps_external_authority_anchor`, 845 `extdeps_model_scope` and 40 `non_fold_residue_frontier` rows are facts whose subject is a file; in the corpus rewrite each moves to the smallest subject it actually governs (a declaration, a namespace prefix, or the compilation subject), with one row per subject and no copies, as part of the corpus homing-and-discharge work item bound to this intention in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_intention_binding`."),
      li(text: "**Layer 4, seed retirement (`v1-emitter-delete`, `v1-interpreter-delete`).** The seed's builtins and flat bare-name pool die with the seed; until then the seed mirrors the loader (layer 0) and any step-two meaning change."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**What the layering says about pace.** Earlier-layer contracts and generator capabilities are reused in later layers. A spelling count neither establishes new library work nor gives a duration: one contract can serve many names, while one spelling can need different contracts at different callers. The seed loader, the generator and genuine semantic exceptions are distinct work. Prioritize the native-seven closure before unrelated corpus names; counts alone cannot establish its remaining effort."),
    h2(text: "4. What this intention does not gate"),
    p(text: "`native-seven` and every landing before production admission. The 2026-11-08 ruling that native-seven depends only on its own closure stands (`gunbc.design_ruling::n7_requires_only_its_own_closure`), and imports remain the binding mechanism until the cut lands (`gunbc.design_ruling::imports_are_the_terminal_name_mechanism`, whose withdrawal of grammar deletion is superseded but whose binding rule is not). The two intentions meet at `native-production-admission`."),
    h2(text: "5. Open questions"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Open: dots for citations too.** `::` lives only in the citation spelling (`std.decl_ref`'s display key, the marker grammar, the sweep); source already uses dots, and zero paths today name both a prefix and a declaration. One structural identity carrier (a nonempty path plus a tagged member coordinate) replaces `DeclarationRef` and `QualifiedName` first; dots are then its one rendering."),
      li(text: "**Settled 2026-11-17: the spelling is the full module path, always** (`gunbc.design_ruling::declaration_references_are_fully_qualified`); a shorter form is later sugar, if ever. The program review's layer-0 finding (global spelling uniqueness is an ambient namespace) is answered by this rule rather than by a candidate-population authority."),
      li(text: "**The interlock milestone.** `NamespaceGrammarRetired` was superseded on 2026-11-08 and is no longer a prerequisite in `gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_interlock`. Re-admitting it as a prerequisite of `SelfHostSeedRetirement` (or of production admission) is a realization act on that carrier, owed by whoever picks this program up, and not done in the plan change that recorded the ruling."),
      li(text: "**Settled 2026-11-19.** At production admission both parsers reject imports and the production route has one active resolver. Interpreter retirement supplies the later proof that the unused mirror has left the tree (`gunbc.design_ruling::production_namespace_admission_precedes_seed_mirror_removal`)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "6. Observation, 2026-11-16: the ambient ledger re-measured"),
    p(text: "The operator asked whether the waves had cleared eight of the ledger's rows. Measured with the ledger's own producer (gunb-ai/gunbc-private#289 `ambient_sweep.py`: a bare site is a call or pipe of a builtin-universe name in a file that neither imports nor declares it, a grep proxy and not the resolver's census) re-run against main at 0b4e665 and joined to the ledger by name, 156 rows join."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Bare sites across the joined rows: 110,228 on 2026-11-08, 117,840 today.** 53 names grew, 19 shrank, one reached zero (`repeat`, two sites). The corpus adds bare sites faster than the waves remove them: `concat` alone added about 2,500 in eight days."),
      li(text: "**Homing versus site migration are different work.** A name can have a declared home under std or extdeps while none of its call sites import it; a home with no caller importing it is a declaration nothing consumes until the sweep that rewrites the sites runs. How many names are homed and how many sites have moved is status, read from the event log, not held here."),
      li(text: "**Inside the native-seven closure** (161 modules by import edges) there are 1,514 bare sites today, and 35 of the 37 ledger names scoped to that closure still have at least one. The largest are the roster-bound higher-order names (fold 617, any 75, filter 62, map 30) and the template-bound pair (concat 212, count 118), which bind natively today through the collection roster and so are not refusals; the names that do refuse are the host-text and map families (discriminant 82, split 38, first 33, starts_with 28, join 25, skip 21, string_length 19, replace 18)."),
      li(text: "**The universe is over-broad.** The ledger's 97 rest-of-corpus rows are mostly host-realized instrument functions with one or two callers (compile_dag_*, doc_graph_*, observed_*), in the universe only because they are exported from the seed's runtime; 36 rows have no callers at all. The names that matter to this intention are the 46 native-seven rows, the five roster-bound higher-order names and the three remaining table arms."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Reading.** Eight of two hundred is the wrong frame in both directions: by homes, about thirty names have a declaration; by sites, essentially none has been cleared, and the total is rising. One name at a time, one PR per home and a hand-picked sweep of a few files each (the Wave A2 and D3 pattern) does not converge against a corpus adding thousands of sites a week. That is the measured case for section 2's generated rewrite as one cut. Not for a ratchet: the operator ruled those out the same day, and the number is watched by the reading in section 7 instead."),
    h2(text: "7. Observation, 2026-11-16: binding bare names to their one known declaration, read by a simple grep"),
    p(text: "The operator's preferred instrument: a deliberately simple reading, used with judgment and falsified by hand, kept with the session rather than enrolled anywhere. For each module it lists every call head the file neither declares nor imports and how many production declarations (fn, data, type, concept, enum under dag and src/v2, test and fixture modules excluded) carry that name. First falsification: the first version counted `fn` and `if` as call heads, counted lambda parameters called as functions, and called `join` unique because one test witness declares a `join`; all three were corrected before the numbers below."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Native-seven closure, 161 modules, bare call heads:** 110 sites of 13 names bind to exactly one production declaration today with no import (decl_ref 23, string_length 19, substring 12, map_insert 12, skip 11, length 10, empty_map 6, char_at 5, string_contains 5); 6 sites of one name are ambiguous (`contains`: std.algebra against gunbc.instruments.router_proxy_falsifier); 1,229 sites of 61 names have no same-spelled declaration in that reading (fold 586, concat 211, count 114, any 45, filter 41, starts_with 28, first 28, split 27, map 20, replace 18, to_string 13, code_point 10, and a tail of one to six sites each). The roster-bound seven bind natively in that reading; the other 54 were unmatched by same-spelling lookup. That reading does not search existing aliases or prove that a new declaration is needed for each name."),
      li(text: "**Would deleting the import lines lose a binding?** Of the native-seven closure's 6,270 import members, 3,902 name a declaration unique in production, 2,300 name a variant constructor the reading does not index, and 68 would become ambiguous without the import: String (v2.std.node against v2.std.text) 22, Int (std.integer against v2.std.integer) 14, contains 9, SourceSpan, TerminationProof, tokenize, IntegerOverflow. Over all 5,910 production modules: 149,854 members, 1,617 ambiguous (about one percent), led by FilePath (std.types against v2.extdeps.file_system) 292, String 176, Int 132, Unit 73, UInt8, PositiveInt. Nearly every collision is a dag std declaration re-declared under src/v2/std, which the 2026-10-18 kernel-type layer rule already forbids (`cross-module-declarations` boundary: compiler-side projections never redeclare); discharging those is the type-name waves H1 to H5, not new work."),
      li(text: "**Variant names:** 409 of 33,933 variant names have more than one production home (Refused 10, Signed 8, the scalar families 7 each). Most are disambiguated by the expected type at a construction; the reading cannot say which are not."),
      li(text: "**The seed-tolerance test did not run.** The seed CLI refuses to run outside a cgroup v2 memory envelope (`gunbc.host.memory_envelope`), and this session's container has none; faking the externally-bounded-executor arm was declined as a bypass of that envelope. The command for a fleet host, baseline then with the entry file's import member lists stripped: `gunbc --dry-run run --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/lexical_scope.dag --function <claim>`, once per claim (29 claims); the seed interpreter reports each claim's Bool in its refusal line, because since the claim-execution cutover no gunbc test route evaluates a src/v2/test/claim module on the interpreter in one process."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Reassessment, 2026-11-19 at 9e9994480d1.** The earlier conclusion that 54 names need new homes is not supported by this same-spelling reading. Source inspection of v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep::roster_head_rows and std.algebra::list_head shows an existing declaration and rewrite for first, including its xs label; list_push already has a compatible home and row. sort_by already has distinct symbol, string and digest-key mappings. Conversely, v2.std.text::string_split takes a nonempty delimiter and a scalar-list String, while gunbc.host.network_install_host_reader::installed_host_machine_id_provisioned calls split with an empty delimiter. That caller needs contract reconciliation, not merely a new path. This is a concrete corpus example, not evidence that the installer belongs to native-seven. The sweep still inserts imports through v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep::roster_import_row_home, so a fully-qualified rewrite is not yet demonstrated by the existing rename rows. These are bounded source observations, not an executed closure census or a fresh duration measurement; the remaining contract population is unresolved."),
    h2(text: "8. Realization"),
    p(text: "The layers of section 3 are realized as work items under the `namespace-unique-on-chain` project, each bound to this intention at its layer in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_intention_binding` and its edges declared in `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority`, so a landing on any of them can be read against the goal it serves. Which item sits at which layer, and its current status, is read from the binding and the event log, not restated here. The work items may be redrawn without this plan changing; what a landing reports is which name moved from no-declaration to unique, which collision was discharged, or which mechanism's inventory reached zero, never a count of files rewritten."),
  ]
}

data names_without_imports_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "names-without-imports",
  title: "Names without imports: every name decided one way, and the import concept gone before v2 is accepted",
  body: names_without_imports_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 1 is achieved: no import grammar, every reference carrying its declaration through the one kernel, the legacy mechanisms at zero, and native-production-admission consuming it.") },
}
